Instructions

Step 1: Assemble the Breadboard

Begin by laying out the breadboard with the rows and columns labeled. You can refer to the breadboard diagram if you are unfamiliar with how to read it.

Step 2: Connect the Power Supply

Connect one end of the 10K resistor to 5V on the Arduino, and the other end to one of the positive power rails (Vin). Connect the other end of the 10K resistor to ground (GND). Connect the positive lead of the RGB LED anode (long leg) to the positive power rail, and the cathode (short leg) to the 10K resistor in series with it.

Step 3: Hook Up the Buzzer

Connect the piezo buzzer between digital pin 9 (PWM) and ground (GND).

Step 4: Test the Circuit

Upload the following code to the Arduino:
```c++
const int LED_R = 12;  // assign pin 12 to the red LED
const int LED_G = 11;  // assign pin 11 to the green LED
const int LED_B = 10;  // assign pin 10 to the blue LED
const int BUZZER = 9;  // assign pin 9 to the piezo buzzer

// constants won't change. They're used here to
// set pin modes:
const int LED_PINS[] = { LED_R, LED_G, LED_B };
const int NUM_LEDS = sizeof(LED_PINS) / sizeof(int);

// variables will change:
int brightness = 0;  // variable for brightness of LED
int delayTime = 500; // variable for delay time
boolean lightEnabled = false; // variable for turning the LED on or off

void setup() {
  // initialize the LED pins:
  for (int thisLED = 0; thisLED < NUM_LEDS; thisLED++) {
    pinMode(LED_PINS[thisLED], OUTPUT);
  }

  pinMode(BUZZER, OUTPUT); // set the piezo buzzer pin to output
}

void loop() {
  digitalWrite(BUZZER, HIGH); // turn the piezo on
  delay(200); // pause for 200 milliseconds
  digitalWrite(BUZZER, LOW); // turn the piezo off
  delay(2000); // pause for 2 seconds

  // change the brightness of the LED:
  if (lightEnabled == true) {
    brightness += 5; // increment brightness by 5

    if (brightness > 255) {
      brightness = 255; // limit the brightness to 255
    }
  }

  // set the color of the LED:
  digitalWrite(LED_PINS[0], brightness); // set the red LED brightness
  digitalWrite(LED_PINS[1], brightness); // set the green LED brightness
  digitalWrite(LED_PINS[2], brightness); // set the blue LED brightness
}
```
