In Spring MVC, the GetMapping annotation is used to map HTTP GET requests to a specific method in a controller class. This annotation is a shorthand for @RequestMapping(method = RequestMethod.GET). The method annotated with @GetMapping processes incoming HTTP GET requests and returns a response in the form of a ModelAndView, ResponseEntity, String, or any other type based on the functionality of the application.

Here's an example of using @GetMapping in a Spring MVC controller:

```java
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.GetMapping;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RestController;

@RestController
public class ExampleController {

    @GetMapping("/example")
    public String getExample() {
        return "This is an example response";
    }
}
```

In this example, when an HTTP GET request is made to the "/example" URL, the getExample() method is executed, which returns a simple String. In other scenarios, you may return a ModelAndView, ResponseEntity, or other data structures based on the needs of your application.

